CORE
main.c
--unwind 6 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Control for `store_through_pointer_lost_update`: the threads do not take
a[i]'s mutex, so one can increment a[i].datum while another asserts it is
0. The stores' own bytes must still be published, so this must stay FAILED
before and after.
